-- examples/checks/ds-tree-explain.rofl — the ds_tree_explain world keeps no witness (`sealed(provenance)`), so the Rust engine answers the closure `dte_w` of the declared tree from the tree and stores none of its rows; its why, why all and the premises an aggregate cell keeps for its members are those of the world that stores the rows.
tree dte_e(P, C) closure dte_w.
sealed(provenance).
dte_e(a, b). dte_e(b, c). dte_e(c, d). dte_e(a, x).
dte_top(D) :- dte_w(a, D).
dte_cnt(N) :- N is count(D : dte_w(a, D)).
